From: Stephender (Antigravity Phase 1 Fix 1b)
Subject: [PATCH] Add physical RAM helper and use it for default undo memory cap

Follow-up to 0001-undo-hardening.patch. Applies on top of
0001-undo-hardening.patch against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1).

The bug:
BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes() does NOT return installed physical RAM:
- source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h:38-41 documents it as "Get maximum
  addressable memory in megabytes" / "(clamped to #INT_MAX)".
- source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc:208-216 computes
  `(size_t(1) << (sizeof(size_t[8]) - 1)) >> 20 * 2` (~16 EiB on 64-bit),
  which is maximum virtual address space, not installed RAM.
- BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int() (system.cc:218-223) clamps that
  to INT_MAX (2,147,483,647 MB).

Because Fix 1 called BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int() / 16 in
BKE_blendfile_userdef_from_defaults(), clamp(ram_mb / 16, 256, 2048) was a
constant 2048 MB on every 64-bit machine (verified live: Fix 1 printed
undo_mem_limit 2048 on both the 7.7 GB Linux VM and the 16 GB Windows CI
runner).

What changed:
- source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h: declare
  BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes() returning physical installed RAM
  in megabytes, explicitly contrasted with BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes.
- source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc: define
  BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes() following Cycles'
  system_physical_ram() pattern (intern/cycles/util/system.cpp:247-266):
  GlobalMemoryStatusEx on Windows (via existing BLI_winstuff.h -> windows.h),
  sysctlbyname("hw.memsize") on macOS (adding <sys/sysctl.h> and <sys/types.h>
  under #if defined(__APPLE__)), and sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE) *
  sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES) on Linux/POSIX (via existing <unistd.h>), plus
  <cstdint> for uint64_t.
- source/blender/blenkernel/intern/blendfile.cc: switch Fix 1's
  userdef->undomemory initialization in BKE_blendfile_userdef_from_defaults()
  to BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes(), keeping clamp(ram_mb / 16,
  256, 2048). Upstream's userdef->memcachelimit line is untouched.

Expected observable difference (factory default undo_mem_limit):
- 16 GB CI runner (16,384 MiB): 1024 MB (was 2048 MB; ~1000-1024 MB if
  firmware reserves a fraction of RAM).
- 8 GB laptop (8,192 MiB): 512 MB (was 2048 MB).
- 4 GB laptop (4,096 MiB): 256 MB (was 2048 MB).
- >=32 GB machine: 2048 MB (clamp max, unchanged).

Note: staged Fix 2 (phase1-fix2-ram-aware-cache.patch) still calls
BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int() and should be updated to use
BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes() in a separate job.

STATUS: STAGED - verified to apply cleanly on top of 0001-undo-hardening.patch
against Blender v5.2.4 (cd5dc428cce1). NOT yet in stephender-repo/patches/.

diff --git a/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/blendfile.cc b/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/blendfile.cc
index 8c9af7e..85676fc 100644
--- a/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/blendfile.cc
+++ b/source/blender/blenkernel/intern/blendfile.cc
@@ -1569,11 +1569,12 @@ UserDef *BKE_blendfile_userdef_from_defaults()
   userdef->memcachelimit = min_ii(BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int() / 2,
                                   userdef->memcachelimit);
 
-  /* Cap default undo stack proportionally to RAM (256 MB on <=4 GB, 512 MB on
-   * 8 GB, up to 2048 MB). The DNA default stays 0 (unlimited) so saved
-   * userpref.blend files that explicitly chose 0 are still respected. */
-  userdef->undomemory = min_ii(max_ii(BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int() / 16, 256),
-                               2048);
+  /* Cap default undo stack proportionally to physical RAM (256 MB on <=4 GB,
+   * 512 MB on 8 GB, 1024 MB on 16 GB, up to 2048 MB). The DNA default stays 0
+   * (unlimited) so saved userpref.blend files that explicitly chose 0 are still
+   * respected. */
+  userdef->undomemory = int(
+      min_zz(max_zz(BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes() / 16, size_t(256)), size_t(2048)));
 
   /* Init weight paint range. */
   BKE_colorband_init(&userdef->coba_weight, true);
diff --git a/source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h b/source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h
index bf7d7e0..b6ec41a 100644
--- a/source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h
+++ b/source/blender/blenlib/BLI_system.h
@@ -39,6 +39,12 @@ void BLI_hostname_get(char *buffer, size_t buffer_maxncpy);
 size_t BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes();
 /** Get maximum addressable memory in megabytes (clamped to #INT_MAX). */
 int BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int();
+/**
+ * Get physical installed RAM in megabytes (returns 0 if unavailable).
+ * Unlike #BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes (which returns maximum addressable
+ * virtual memory), this queries actual physical system RAM.
+ */
+size_t BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes();
 
 /**
  * Ensure the process can open many files simultaneously.
diff --git a/source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc b/source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc
index 473457d..e36bf0f 100644
--- a/source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc
+++ b/source/blender/blenlib/intern/system.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <climits>
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <cstdio>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstring>
@@ -28,6 +29,10 @@
 #  if defined(HAVE_EXECINFO_H)
 #    include <execinfo.h>
 #  endif
+#  if defined(__APPLE__)
+#    include <sys/sysctl.h>
+#    include <sys/types.h>
+#  endif
 #  include <sys/resource.h>
 #  include <unistd.h>
 #endif
@@ -222,6 +227,32 @@ int BLI_system_memory_max_in_megabytes_int()
   return int(min_zz(limit_megabytes, size_t(INT_MAX)));
 }
 
+size_t BLI_system_memory_physical_in_megabytes()
+{
+#if defined(WIN32)
+  MEMORYSTATUSEX ram = {};
+  ram.dwLength = sizeof(ram);
+  if (GlobalMemoryStatusEx(&ram)) {
+    return size_t(ram.ullTotalPhys >> 20);
+  }
+  return 0;
+#elif defined(__APPLE__)
+  uint64_t ram = 0;
+  size_t len = sizeof(ram);
+  if (sysctlbyname("hw.memsize", &ram, &len, nullptr, 0) == 0) {
+    return size_t(ram >> 20);
+  }
+  return 0;
+#else
+  const long page_size = sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE);
+  const long phys_pages = sysconf(_SC_PHYS_PAGES);
+  if (page_size > 0 && phys_pages > 0) {
+    return size_t((uint64_t(page_size) * uint64_t(phys_pages)) >> 20);
+  }
+  return 0;
+#endif
+}
+
 void BLI_system_max_open_files_ensure()
 {
   /* The Windows maximum is documented as 8192. */
